      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Oriental cholangitis is a common illness among immigrants from Southeast Asia. It is distinct from typical western cholangitis, and it is easily misdiagnosed unless a high index of suspicion is maintained. After stabilization with appropriate antimicrobial therapy, surgical drainage of the biliary tree is often advocated."},
